            "title": "Oil posts 8% weekly loss on potential OPEC+ supply additions",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "HOUSTON (Reuters) -Oil prices settled higher on Friday but posted a weekly loss of 8.1% after news of potential increases to OPEC+ supply.  Brent crude futures closed up 42 cents, or 0.7%, at $64.53 a barrel by, while U.S. West Texas Intermediate crude was up 40 cents, or 0.7%, at $60.88.  For the week, Brent fell 8.1%, the largest weekly loss in over three months.",
